uage":null,"source":"anilist","spoiler":false,"text":"High school freshman Hiromi joins the tennis club because of her admiration for Ryuuzaki. Ryuuzaki is a senior, who's the best tennis player on the team and also nicknamed \"Ochoufujin\", (\"Madame Butterfly\"), because of her elegance on the tennis court. However, the new coach, Jin Munakata, wants the inexperienced Hiromi to play in a forthcoming tournament.\n\nDue to this, Hiromi considers quitting tennis for good but, in the depth of her soul, she soon realizes that she loves tennis after all. She returns to the club and, under Munakata's coaching, her talent starts to bloom.\n\nIn the end, Hiromi develops a strong emotional bond with her coach, not knowing that Munakata is risking his life because of a chronic illness.\n\n(Source: AnimeNfo)"},"tags":[{"name":"Tennis","rank":80,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Shoujo","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Female Protagonist","rank":65,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Urban","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Tragedy","rank":50,"spoiler":true}],"titles":{"display":"Aim for the Ace!: The Movie","english":"Aim for the Ace!: The Movie","native":"エースをねらえ！","romaji":"Ace wo Nerae! (1979)","synonyms":[{"language":"zh","source":"bangumi","value":"网球甜心 剧场版"},{"language":null,"source":"bangumi","value":"网球娇娃 剧场版"},{"language":null,"source":"bangumi","value":"エースをねらえ! 劇場版"}]},"trailer":null,"visibility":"general"}